there's no way your name's dr otto  octavious spider-man no way home blew  open the multiverse and our minds  between the crazy stunts breathtaking  cgi and chemistry between all the actors  on set the behind the scenes of no way  home is a sight to behold number one the  arrival of doc ock on the bridge is an  exciting and epic moment and the fight  between him and spider-man is equally  thrilling the filmmakers achieved this  awesome set piece by using a mix of  practical and visual effects  some of the cars being crushed and the  bridge being destroyed was done  practically on a giant blue screen set  and that explosion caused by green  goblin's pumpkin bomb all real digital  effects were used to enhance the scene  and create the rest of the environment  number two when spider-man stole the  return device from doctor strange we  knew there was about to be some awesome  action tom holland was hooked up to  wires to perform the stunts in the scene  which were then digitally removed in  editing holland practiced his car  jumping stun on a golf cart before  taking it in front of the cameras  cumberbatch was thoroughly impressed  with the work put in by the filmmakers  as were we the scale of what they have  is not to be underestimated number three  did you know that willem dafoe is  something of a stuntman himself defoe  was adamant that if he was going to  reprise his role as the iconic green  goblin he was to do as many of his own  stunts as possible i don't want to just  pop in there i want to do the action  because that's fun for me during the  spider-man green goblin fight scene in  the apartment building they actually  broke through multiple levels of  flooring the set was built specifically  for this stunt with blue screen lining  the halls for the cgi to fill in the  rest of the building  number four doc ox mechanical tentacles  were completely cgi in no way home a  huge difference from when alfred molina  first played the character in sam  raimi's spider-man 2. back then the arms  were physical props that were  puppeteered molina welcomed the new vfx  technology with open arms no pun  intended and he loved how they created  the appendages digitally you know it's  familiar but at the same time completely  new because the technology has moved on  molina was hooked up to a toothpick rig  to simulate the metal arms carrying him  around which made for some funny  behind-the-scenes moments we're chatting  and then all of a sudden he would just  kind of disappear  number five when doctor strange casts  the spell that kicks off the main  journey of the film he does so in a  dungy basement that he lights up with  the spell on set the basement was real  and they used circling lights to  simulate the light of the spell being  cast the round floating table that the  spell is cast on was held on a green  pole and also had circling lights on it  after some cgi magic the spell casting  scene was complete  number six tom and zendaya spent a lot  of time in this film falling from  heights one of their falls had them  jumping off of a very high up blue  platform while attached to a wire that  platform would later change into a metal  beam high up in the new york city air  with the help of cgi but that jump was  very real i mean i don't love heights  but i've learned to over you know the  last six years playing this character  number seven the incredible finale of no  way home took place at a modified statue  of liberty that held captain america  shield the very top of the statue was a  practical set as were parts of the base  everything else though was created with  a whole lot of cgi to complete this  climactic set piece  number eight that angry mob that is  present when peter and his friends are  going to school very real the rest of  the world not so much cgi was used to  create anything in the surrounding area  that wasn't the school you may be  wondering why they would go through all  that trouble the answer is this movie  was shot in atlanta georgia not new york  so any scenes with new york landscaping  in the background was 100  cgi we down here in georgia baby down  here in georgia number nine it's such a  simple scene that takes place in a  coffee shop how can there be cgi well  it's because of what we just explained  since filming was done in georgia cgi  had to be used to properly replicate new  york city so the inside of the coffee  shop is real but outside the windows  were giant blue screens where the new  york city street would be added in  post-production it would have been so  nice for them to go to college number 10  i don't think it will surprise anyone to  learn that the mirror dimension is  completely created with cgi however some  parts of the trippy sequence were filmed  on practical sets spider-man doing a  flip onto a warping building was tom  holland actually performing that move on  a beam and the subway trains that were  flying through the grand canyon were  shot using a small trained set piece  with tom holland and benedict  cumberbatch performing on top of it now  if only we could figure out how  spider-man did all that math so quickly  we have nothing but admiration for every  single person that brought spider-man no  way home to life the amount of detailed  cgi throughout the film is an impressive  feat and earned the film an oscar  nomination for best visual effects which  scene do you think had the best cgi  comment down below and let us know
 

